# Finished track, hidden from the user

The owner locked this list. A beginner gets a finished track in a few taps. The studio does the craft. Do not add a compressor, LUFS target, swing percent, EQ, or sample browser to the first screen.

The user sees only: direction and mood, one short phrase or their own dry recording, the shelf wish, section up/down/mute, and download. The card shows measured LUFS, true peak, and low/mid/air. An unmeasured number stays «—».

Do not ship a formant voice as a singer. Do not claim a mix was split into the original synths. Do not copy a reference melody. Do not invent loudness or 128 BPM.

The engine does this work. It is not the Beatport bar in `studio-beatport-bar.mdc`. There is still no knob for it. Three limits stay honest: swing is chosen by the section, because the file analysis has no measured swing; the card prints the real LUFS, peak, and air, even when loudness is quieter than −9…−7 or the top band is absent; a dry phrase is still «сухое произнесение», not a singer. Stem files, when the browser can render them together, sum to the file on the card. An Ableton export of our own track and a 48 kHz video file stay later work.

Hidden work, in this order:

1. Club drum one-shots, not a sine plus noise.
2. A house kit plays unless the user brought their own sound.
3. Bass and hook presets with unison and envelopes, no preset menu.
4. A second musical idea inside 10:00, not one 8-note loop.
5. A bass phrase, not only the root.
6. Chord changes, not one held note.
7. Section groove, not one fixed swing, and not a measured copy of the reference.
8. Shaker, ride, crash, and toms placed by the section.
9. Reverse cymbal, impact, and downlifter at the joints.
10. One room and one delay, chosen by section, with no send knobs.
11. Real top-end energy so the card can show air when it is actually there.
12. A performance of the user's phrase. Their words stay the only vocal input.
13. A second phrase only when their text has one. No invented verse.
14. Double, harmony, and breath done inside the mix.
15. The lyric sheet stays text. One short phrase can enter the track.
16. A foreign vocal is never pulled out of a finished record.
17. Drop question and answer, a one-beat kick gap, no extra screens.
18. Two themes across 10:00.
19. Section moves stay the timeline. No bar editor on the first screen.
20. Notes stay internal. The piano roll stays a picture.
21. Their file lands only through the shelf or the dry-phrase drop.
22. A longer drop writes new bars. It does not only steal bars from a neighbor.
23. Master stays one chain: EQ, clip, and the −1.0 dBTP ceiling. No mix console.
24. Density high enough that measured loudness can reach about −9…−7 LUFS without passing the peak ceiling.
25. Sidechain amount follows the section.
26. Low end under 100 Hz stays mono. No correlation meter on the card.
27. Drum notes stay out of the user MIDI until a real kit exists.
28. Stem download, when added, must sum to the same master.
29. The card meter stays an estimate. Do not call it a certified plant meter.
30. Kick, hat, bass, space, and swing have no knobs.
31. Shelf character changes the next track. It does not become a synth extractor.
32. A finished mix is never described as separated stems.
33. «Мелодичнее» and «Профессиональнее» change the next render. The drop loop is the audition.
34. Reference match only turns the louder file down.
35. A 10:00 24-bit WAV stays a disk download when it is over 50 MB. Say that in one sentence.
36. An Ableton project of our track is a later export, not a first-screen tool.
37. Render stays in the browser. A phone that cannot hold 10:00 is told before the render starts.
38. Music delivery stays 44.1 kHz. A 48 kHz video file is a separate later delivery.
